# the argument of mill-proof.md by rule (phil/skeleton): connectives from the parse, an atom to each clause
atom	people_actually_see(x)	x: is that people actually see it
atom	proof_sound_audible	the only proof that a sound is audible is that people hear it and so of the other sources of our experience
atom	manner_apprehend_sole	in like manner I apprehend the sole evidence it is possible to produce that anything is desirable is that people do actually desire it
atom	end_utilitarian_doctrine(x)	x: if the end which the utilitarian doctrine proposes to itself were not in theory and in practice acknowledged to be an end could ever convince any person that it was so
atom	given_general_happiness(x)	x: can be given why the general happiness is desirable except that each person so far as he believes it to be attainable desires his own happiness
atom	reason(x)	x: reason
atom	fact_proof_case	this however being a fact we have not only all the proof which the case admits of but all which it is possible to require that happiness is a good that each person's happiness is a good to that person and the general happiness therefore a good to the aggregate of all persons
atom	made_title_end(x)	x: has made out its title as one of the ends of conduct and consequently one of the criteria of morality
P1	S1	people_actually_see(proof_capable_object)
P2	S2	proof_sound_audible
P3	S3	manner_apprehend_sole
P4	S4	(all x: !end_utilitarian_doctrine(x))
P5	S5	(all x: reason(x) -> !given_general_happiness(x))
P6	S6	fact_proof_case
C	S7	made_title_end(happiness)
# rules tool=phil/skeleton date=2026-10-20
